{"id": "5c1053a5-d08e-4960-8c5b-4b8fbb1ef084", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T14:14:29.654216", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "84c54b38-5c94-4e42-a428-819460d88bec", "action": null, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "call-426a501e-82cc-42cb-85fc-f8f6d253085e", "tool_call": {"id": "call-426a501e-82cc-42cb-85fc-f8f6d253085e", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "execute_check", "arguments": "{"summary":"Write entry-point docs (README, DESIGN, LICENSE_NOTES, OPEN_QUESTIONS)","command":"cat > README.md << 'EOF'\n# Size vs Alignment in LLaMA-2 — Experiment Design (design-only)\n\n## Research questions (RQs)\n\n- **RQ1 (monotonicity).** Within LLaMA-2 family, do quality metrics grow monotonically with parameter count (7B → 13B → 70B) under controlled inference (decoding, prompt template, few-shot count)?\n- **RQ2 (interaction).** Is there a statistically significant `size × alignment` interaction term (β_interact ≠ 0)? Positive ⇒ alignment amplifies the size effect; negative or large positive β_alignment with small β_size ⇒ alignment substitutes for size.\n- **RQ3 (pretrain gating).** Does the size effect survive when pretrain data/FLOPs are held constant — i.e., when comparing the Pythia family (fixed The Pile, fixed steps, sizes 1B/6.9B/12B)? Is the Pythia slope comparable in magnitude to the LLaMA-2 slope?\n- **RQ4 (alignment strata).** Do effects differ across (a) alignment-neutral benchmarks (MMLU/ARC-C/GSM8K/BBH/HumanEval) and (b) alignment-sensitive benchmarks (TruthfulQA/IFEval/ToxiGen)?\n- **RQ5 (historical anchor).** Where does LLaMA-1-65B-base sit on the size axis when pretrain lacks RLHF and is older — does its profile look more like a bigger-base or like a chat model on alignment-sensitive metrics?\n\n## Pre-stated hypotheses\n\n- **H1 (size dominates):** β_size > 0; β_alignment small; β_interact small. Monotonic growth regardless of alignment.\n- **H2 (alignment buys size back):** Smaller chat model can surpass larger base model on alignment-sensitive metrics (e.g., LLaMA-2-7B-chat ≥ LLaMA-2-13B-base on IFEval/TruthfulQA). β_alignment > 0 large; per-stratum model shows β_interact positive on alignment-sensitive cells.\n- **H3 (pretrain gates size):** Pythia β_size is *weaker* in absolute slope than LLaMA-2's, indicating that some of LLaMA-2's \"size effect\" is really compute/data effect.\n\n## Deliverables (this directory)\n\nDesign-only package. No experiment was executed; numerical cells are placeholders (`TBD`).\n\n| Path | Contents |\n| --- | --- |\n| [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md) | full narrative: factors, anchors, benchmarks, statistical plan |\n| [LICENSE_NOTES.md](LICENSE_NOTES.md) | licensing & weights-access notes |\n| [OPEN_QUESTIONS.md](OPEN_QUESTIONS.md) | residual uncertainties for the researcher |\n| [conditions/](conditions/) | 9-cell table (6 LLaMA-2 × {base,chat} + 3 Pythia base + LLaMA-1-65B base) |\n| [protocol/](protocol/) | decoding settings, chat templates, prompting rules |\n| [benchmarks/](benchmarks/) | benchmark mapping, contamination gating, subsampling, strata |\n| [stats/](stats/) | regression, multiplicity, pairwise contrasts, sample size, plots |\n| [report_template/](report_template/) | report skeleton with pairwise-difference tables and plot recipes |\n| [reproducibility/](reproducibility/) | checklist and environment lock |\n\n## Scope\n\nDesign-only. No benchmarks queried, no weights loaded, no inference run. Execution would require ≥1×H100 80GB per 70B run plus access to Meta-licensed weights (see [LICENSE_NOTES.md](LICENSE_NOTES.md)).\n\n## Reading order\n\n1. [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md) for the full design rationale.\n2. [conditions/conditions_table.md](conditions/conditions_table.md) for the cell grid.\n3. [protocol/](protocol/) for what would actually be run.\n4. [benchmarks/](benchmarks/) for what would actually be measured.\n5. [stats/](stats/) for the inferential machinery.\n6. [report_template/REPORT.md](report_template/REPORT.md) for the output skeleton.\nEOF\n\necho \"wrote README.md\"\n\ncat > DESIGN.md << 'EOF'\n# Full Design Narrative — Size × Alignment × Pretrain in LLaMA-2\n\n## 1. The question, decomposed\n\nThe public task asks whether *parameter count* per se is sufficient to improve performance, or whether **insufficient pretraining** and **missing alignment** can erase (or invert) the size benefit. The question as posed conflates three factors:\n\n1. **P** — number of parameters,\n2. **T** — pretraining recipe (data scale + compute + curriculum),\n3. **A** — alignment stage (SFT, RLHF, none).\n\nWithin publicly released weights of LLaMA-2 only, P and T are highly correlated: the 70B was trained with more tokens than the 7B in terms of expected compute-optimal scaling, but Meta's released card does not let us hold T constant and vary P. Two complementary moves address this: (i) bring in a **controlled-pretrain anchor family** (Pythia), and (ii) include a **historical anchor** (LLaMA-1-65B-base) to display pretrain vintage effects.\n\n## 2. Design overview\n\n### 2.1 Primary factorial\n\n```\nCells 1..6 (LLaMA-2)\n  size      ∈ {7B, 13B, 70B}\n  alignment ∈ {base, chat}\n\nCells 7..9 (Pythia; fixed pretrain under The Pile, identical steps)\n  size      ∈ {1B, 6.9B, 12B}\n  alignment = base\n\nAnchor (Cell 10)\n  LLaMA-1-65B base\n```\n\n### 2.2 What each cell accomplishes\n\n- **Within LLaMA-2** (cells 1..6): the focal test for the public question. Yields β_size, β_alignment, β_interact.\n- **Pythia** (cells 7..9): pure β_size with controlled pretrain. If Pythia's slope equals LLaMA-2's, the LLaMA-2 size effect is mostly **parameter-driven**; if Pythia's is shallower, the LLaMA-2 size effect package includes a non-trivial training-compute component.\n- **LLaMA-1-65B** (anchor): shows where an older, no-alignment, not-newline-trained large model lands on the same axis; mainly a sanity/data-drift visual.\n\n## 3. Benchmark selection and stratification\n\nBenchmarks are split into two strata a priori (declared, not data-adaptive):\n\n**Alignment-neutral** (knowledge, reasoning, code — should respond mostly to P, weakly to A):\n- MMLU (5-shot; logprob/MC accuracy)\n- ARC-C (0-shot)\n- GSM8K (8-shot; maj@1/5)\n- HumanEval (pass@1/10 with n=5/10 samples)\n- BBH (3-shot, all 27 subtasks)\n\n**Alignment-sensitive** (instruction following, truthfulness, toxicity):\n- TruthfulQA (MC2, logprob-based)\n- IFEval (strict/loose accuracy)\n- ToxiGen (implicit-toxic, classifier-scored)\n\n**Optional, gated** (require local judge, see §7):\n- MT-Bench (judge: `prometheus-2-8x7b-instruct` or `llama-3-70b-instruct`)\n- AlpacaEval (same judge conditions)\n\nStratification is *declared* in DESIGN before any measurement, so that it is not selected on outcome.\n\n## 4. Protocol fixes (held constant across cells)\n\n- **Decoding.** Default T=0 greedy for non-generative. Generative decoding (GSM8K maj@5, HumanEval pass@k, ToxiGen): T=0.7, top-p=0.95, fixed seed set {17, 23, 29, 31, 37}.\n- **Prompting.** Same `instruction` text for every cell. Chat wraps to Llama-2 chat template; base uses raw text.\n- **Few-shot.** Number of shots fixed per benchmark (see `benchmarks/benchmark_map.yaml`).\n- **Engine.** vLLM or TGI at a pinned version; KV-cache dtype auto; TP=2 only for 70B if a single GPU is <80 GB.\n- **Tokenizer.** Exact commit from the official HF mirror.\n- **Subsampling.** Stratified subsampling at fixed seed for benchmarks > N_max (2048 by default); see `benchmarks/subsampling_strategy.md`.\n\n## 5. Statistical machinery\n\n### 5.1 Cell-level\nFor every (cell × benchmark), report\n\n- mean score s_c, with **paired bootstrap 95% CI** (B=1000).\n- For generative: aggregate over n samples per item, bootstrap items.\n\n### 5.2 Pairwise contrasts\nFor each pair (c_a, c_b):\n\n- Δ = s_c_a − s_c_b (paired on items),\n- 95% CI via paired bootstrap; permutation p-value with 1000 permutations.\n\nRequired per-benchmark contrast sets:\n- Δ(70B−13B), Δ(70B−7B), Δ(13B−7B), each in {base, chat} ⇒ 6 contrasts per benchmark.\n\n### 5.3 Regression (the Q's anchor)\n\nPer benchmark (and per stratum), fit on cells of model family F:\n\n```\ns_c = β0 + β_size · log10(P_c) + β_alignment · z_c + β_interact · log10(P_c) · z_c + ε_c\n```\n\nWeighted by 1/Var(s_c) to favor cells with tighter CIs. Bootstrap CIs on βs by re-fitting within sampled items. Interpretation:\n\n- **β_size** - marginal effect of log-params at base alignment.\n- **β_alignment** - chat vs base at median size.\n- **β_interact** - extra slope added by chat. **H2 predicts β_interact > 0 on the alignment-sensitive stratum.**\n\nStratified refits:\n- on alignment-neutral subset,\n- on alignment-sensitive subset.\n\nThe Pythia-only model (cells 7..9) yields the \"controlled pretrain\" β_size.\n\n### 5.4 Multiplicity\n\nTwo test families; **Benjamini-Hochberg FDR at α = 0.05 within each family**, plus unadjusted p for transparency:\n\n- **Family A**: pairwise contrasts (3 size-diffs × 2 alignment-states = 6 per benchmark).\n- **Family B**: regression βs (3 per benchmark).\n- **Family C** (when included): optional-judge benchmarks isolated to their own BH family to avoid cross-judge FPR mixing.\n\nDecision states:\n- *Confirmed*: p_uncorr < α AND q_BH < 0.05.\n- *Suggestive*: p_uncorr < α, q_BH ≥ 0.05.\n- *No signal*: p_uncorr ≥ α.\n\nA finding is \"advanced\" only if confirmed **and** directionally consistent in the within-stratum and (where applicable) within-Pythia models.\n\n## 6. Contamination gating\n\nMandatory gating before any cell-level number is allowed into the report:\n\n- 13-gram shingles of each benchmark's `question ⊕ reference_answer` strings.\n- Probe against pretrain corpora (LLaMA-2: as released, with our own overlay; Pythia: The Pile; LLaMA-1: CC dumps).\n- Thresholds:\n  - `< 1e-4` — include; flag in report.\n  - `1e-4 ≤ rate < 1e-2` — primary analysis on filtered subset; report filtered + unfiltered.\n  - `≥ 1e-2` — exclude from primary; sensitivity only.\n\nDetail in `benchmarks/contamination_screen.md`.\n\n## 7. Optional judge benchmarks (MT-Bench, AlpacaEval)\n\nBy default *excluded* (network-off environment in the design stage). If included at execution:\n\n- Local judge: **`prometheus-2-8x7b`** (open weights, designed to emulate GPT-4-judge scoring), with `llama-3-70b-instruct` as second opinion.\n- Explicit limitations section: judge self-similarity (Llama-2 judged by Llama-3 raises style overlap), verbosity bias (controlled by length-normalising wins), position bias (rotate A/B and combine).\n- Computed in **Family C** of BH — not pooled with Families A/B.\n\n## 8. Threats to validity (anticipated)\n\n- **Size × training-FLOPs confounding (LLaMA-2):** mitigated by Pythia anchor.\n- **Alignment-data heterogeneity across sizes:** partially mitigable by reading Meta release notes; residual untreated in main analysis, surfaced in limitations.\n- **Benchmark contamination:** gating step.\n- **Decoding variance on generative metrics:** fixed seed set, n ≥ 5 for stochastic tasks.\n- **Tokenizer differences across families:** Pythia vs LLaMA-2 have different tokenizers and dataset mixes; we only compare *families* via relative slopes, not absolute scores.\n- **Optional-judge bias:** see §7.\n- **Bootstrap assumption (independence across items):** LLaMA-2-eval benchmarks vary; sensitivity check by leaving-N-out, not blocking on first 10% vs last 10%, etc.\n\n## 9. Mapping RQs to artifacts\n\n| RQ | Primary artifact |\n| --- | --- |\n| RQ1 | `report_template/REPORT.md` §3 (size main effects) and `stats/pairwise_contrasts.md` |\n| RQ2 | `stats/regression_spec.md` β_interact and `stats/interaction_plots.md` |\n| RQ3 | Pythia-only model in `stats/regression_spec.md`; figure in `stats/interaction_plots.md` |\n| RQ4 | stratum analyses in `stats/regression_spec.md` and `benchmarks/alignment_subsets.md` |\n| RQ5 | narrative placement in `report_template`; LLaMA-1-65B is single point, not in regression |\nEOF\n\necho \"wrote DESIGN.md\"\n\ncat > LICENSE_NOTES.md << 'EOF'\n# License & weights-access notes (design-stage reference, no execution implied)\n\nAll weights access is documented here so that an executor can verify before running. No code or data are downloaded in this design-only stage.\n\n| Family | Component | Repo / source | License / terms | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| LLaMA-2 | base + chat (7B/13B/70B) | `meta-llama/Llama-2-{7b,13b,70b}{,-hf}` and `-chat-hf` mirrors | **Llama-2 Community License** | Requires accepted Meta license on HF. Restricts commercial use above 700M MAU; research use permitted. Hash + commit to be locked at execution (see `reproducibility/environment_lock.md`). |\n| Pythia | base (1B/6.9B/12B), step 143000 | `EleutherAI/pythia-{1b,6.9b,12b}` | **Apache-2.0** | Step is fixed per design; intermediate steps not used. |\n| LLaMA-1 | 65B base | `huggyllama/llama-65b` | **Non-commercial research only** (Meta release terms). | Used as anchor only; not for any production path. |\n\n## Benchmark / dataset licenses\n\n| Benchmark | Source | License / terms |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| MMLU | `cais/mmlu` | MIT |\n| ARC-C | `allenai/ai2_arc` | CC-BY-SA-4.0 |\n| GSM8K | `openai/gsm8k` | MIT |\n| HumanEval | `openai/openai_humaneval` | MIT |\n| BBH | mirror of BIG-Bench Hard | Apache-2.0 (BIG-Bench) |\n| TruthfulQA | `truthful_qa` | Apache-2.0 |\n| IFEval | `google/IFEval` | Apache-2.0 (per card) |\n| ToxiGen | `toxigen/toxigen-data` | Research only; no harm-distribution redistribution |\n| MT-Bench | `lmsys/mt_bench_human_judgments` | CC-BY-NC-4.0 |\n| AlpacaEval | `tatsu-lab/alpaca_eval` | CC-BY-NC-4.0 |\n| The Pile (Pythia pretrain) | `monology/pile-uncopyrighted` | Various; consult dataset card for per-component terms |\n\n## Disallowed-use safeguards\n\n- No prompt designed to elicit harmful content beyond the implicit-evaluation surface of ToxiGen.\n- TruthfulQA / ToxiGen raw generations stored under controlled bucket only; report uses aggregated scores; do not redistribute full outputs in `OPEN` artefacts.\n- LLaMA-1 outputs are not redistributed.\n\n## Pre-execution gate\n\nBefore any execution, the executor must:\n1. Confirm Meta license is on file for the operator.\n2. Confirm benign-use clauses for each benchmark dataset.\n3. Confirm `reproducibility/CHECKLIST.md` items marked \"license\".\nEOF\n\necho \"wrote LICENSE_NOTES.md\"\n\ncat > OPEN_QUESTIONS.md << 'EOF'\n# Open questions for the researcher\n\n1. **Subsample cap.** Default `N_max = 2048` for MMLU/BBH; is a larger cap (e.g., 4096 or full) budget-feasible? Larger N cuts CI width (see `stats/sample_size.md`).\n2. **Optional judge benchmark inclusion.** Include MT-Bench/AlpacaEval at execution? Which local judge is approved (`prometheus-2-8x7b` vs `llama-3-70b-instruct`)?\n3. **Pythia step.** All Pythia anchors use step 143000. Acceptable to also report deduped-step 100000/200000 for sensitivity?\n4. **LLaMA-1 caveats.** LLaMA-1 is non-commercial; can the executor legally run it on the target cluster? If not, substitute with a 2nd anchor family (e.g., Falcon-40B-base) — design choice to be confirmed.\n5. **Δ(70B−13B) vs Pythia slope.** Since LLaMA-2's 70B and 13B differ in pretrain compute, we may want a *delta-vs-Pythia* slope comparison (Pythia-only β_size subtracted). Is that the desired primary test for H3, or should it stay as Pythia-only fit vs LLaMA-2 fit separately?\n6. **ToxiGen classifier.** `toxigen-roberta` is the canonical classifier; ok or substitute (e.g., `roberta-hate-speech-dynabench-r4`)?\n7. **Multiple-testing budget.** Family A (6 pairwise per benchmark), Family B (3 βs per benchmark), Family C (4 βs per optional benchmark). Pooling across *benchmarks* within a family is not currently set; confirm.\n8. **Pretrain-contamination screen thresholds.** Three thresholds proposed in `benchmarks/contamination_screen.md`. Sensible for this study, or tighter/looser?\n9. **Strata definitions.** A-leaky benchmarks: `HumanEval` arguably has prompt-induction effects; `BBH` includes at least one alignment-leaning task. Is the proposed allocation (`alignment_neutral`/`alignment_sensitive`) acceptable as declared, or do you want sub-stratification?\n10. **Interaction plot axes.** Plot on `log10(params)` raw or scale to z within family? Default is raw; z-scaling makes β_size interpretable but obscures the original axis.\nEOF\n\necho \"wrote OPEN_QUESTIONS.md\"\n\nls -la"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-efe1fa3d-8671-42eb-af93-eaac213c25a5", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 17}
