ontamination gating (mandatory)\n\nBefore any cell-level number is allowed into the report:\n\n- 13-gram shingles of every benchmark item's `instruction \u2295 reference_answer` strings.\n- Probe against pretrain corpora:\n  - LLaMA-2 \u2014 Meta's released card claims exclusion of known benchmarks; we additionally run our own overlay probe.\n  - Pythia \u2014 directly probe The Pile (PubMed Central, GitHub, Books, StackExchange, ArXiv \u2026).\n  - LLaMA-1 \u2014 published CC dumps where available.\n- Thresholds (per benchmark):\n  - `rate < 1e-4` \u2014 include; flag in report.\n  - `1e-4 \u2264 rate < 1e-2` \u2014 primary analysis on filtered subset; report filtered + unfiltered.\n  - `rate \u2265 1e-2` \u2014 exclude from primary; sensitivity only.\n\nSee `benchmarks/contamination_screen.md`.\n\n## 7. Optional judge benchmarks (MT-Bench, AlpacaEval)\n\nDefault *excluded*. If included at execution:\n\n- Local judge preferred: **`prometheus-2-8x7b-instruct`** (open weights, designed to emulate GPT-4-judge scoring), with **`llama-3-70b-instruct`** as second opinion.\n- Limitations section in report must include:\n  - judge self-similarity (Llama-2-(-chat) judged by Llama-3 raises style overlap);\n  - verbosity bias (controlled by length-normalised win-rate on AlpacaEval);\n  - position bias (rotate A/B, average).\n\nComputed in **Family C** of BH; not pooled with Families A/B.\n\n## 8. Threats to validity (declared)\n\n1. **P \u00d7 training-FLOPs confounding (LLaMA-2):** mitigated by Pythia anchor.\n2. **Alignment-data heterogeneity across sizes:** partially mitigable via Meta release notes; residual unmodelled in main analysis, surfaced in limitations.\n3. **Benchmark contamination:** gating step.\n4. **Decoding variance on generative metrics:** fixed seed set, n \u2265 5 for stochastic tasks.\n5. **Tokenizer differences across families:** Pythia vs LLaMA-2 differ; compare families via *relative slopes*, not absolute scores.\n6. **Optional-judge bias:** see \u00a77.\n7. **Bootstrap item-independence assumption:** sensitivity check by leaving-one-out and prefix-vs-suffix N (TBD).\n\n## 9. Mapping RQs \u2192 artifacts\n\n| RQ | Primary artifact | Secondary artifact |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| RQ1 | `stats/pairwise_contrasts.md` Tables S1\u2013S3 | `report_template/REPORT.md` \u00a73 |\n| RQ2 | `stats/regression_spec.md` \u03b2_interact | `stats/interaction_plots.md` |\n| RQ3 | Pythia-only model in `stats/regression_spec.md` | `stats/interaction_plots.md` Pythia panel |\n| RQ4 | stratum analyses in `stats/regression_spec.md` | `benchmarks/alignment_subsets.md` |\n| RQ5 | LLaMA-1-65B single-point overlay | `stats/interaction_plots.md` anchor row |\nEOF\necho \"wrote DESIGN.md ($(wc -c < DESIGN.md) bytes)\""}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-0f043a81-c593-41da-966b-efe13a8523a4", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 21}
