ata` | Research-only; no harm-distribution redistribution |\n| MT-Bench | `lmsys/mt_bench_human_judgments` | CC-BY-NC-4.0 |\n| AlpacaEval | `tatsu-lab/alpaca_eval` | CC-BY-NC-4.0 |\n| The Pile (Pythia pretrain) | `monology/pile-uncopyrighted` | Mix of per-component terms; consult dataset card |\n\n## Disallowed-use safeguards\n\n- No prompt designed to elicit harmful content beyond the implicit-evaluation surface of ToxiGen.\n- TruthfulQA / ToxiGen raw generations stored under controlled bucket only; report uses aggregated scores; full outputs are not redistributed in `OPEN` artefacts.\n- LLaMA-1 outputs are not redistributed and the model is referenced for analysis only.\n\n## Pre-execution gate\n\nBefore any execution, the executor must:\n1. Confirm Meta Llama-2 license is on file for the operator (and, separately, for LLaMA-1's non-commercial clause).\n2. Confirm benign-use clauses for each benchmark dataset (ToxiGen in particular).\n3. Sign off `reproducibility/CHECKLIST.md` items marked \"license\".\n4. Confirm that the chosen local judge weights are accessible under their own license.\nEOF\necho \"wrote LICENSE_NOTES.md ($(wc -c < LICENSE_NOTES.md) bytes)\"\n\ncat > OPEN_QUESTIONS.md << 'EOF'\n# Open questions for the researcher\n\nThese are residual questions that can plausibly be left open at execution time, but they should be tracked.\n\n1. **Subsample cap.** Default `N_max = 2048` for MMLU and BBH. Is a larger cap (e.g., 4096 or full) budget-feasible? Larger N cuts CI width (see `stats/sample_size.md`).\n2. **Optional judge benchmark inclusion.** Include MT-Bench and AlpacaEval at execution? Which local judge is approved (`prometheus-2-8x7b-instruct` vs `llama-3-70b-instruct`)?\n3. **Pythia step.** All Pythia anchors use step 143000. Acceptable to also report deduped-step 100000 / 200000 for sensitivity?\n4. **LLaMA-1 caveats.** LLaMA-1 is non-commercial; can the executor legally run it on the target cluster? If not, substitute with a 2nd anchor family (e.