{"id": "ed86a652-99d2-4b0a-9050-d671b8243502", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T14:15:43.386446", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "41aed133-45ed-405f-83b7-9f33d4ca7296", "action": {"command": "cat > conditions/conditions_table.md << 'EOF'
# Conditions / cells

The experimental unit is `(model_cell, benchmark)`. Total: **10 cells × 11 benchmarks (8 required + 3 optional)**

## 10 model cells

Aliases used in all downstream tables.

| # | alias | family | params (B) | tokens (T) | alignment | source repo | license | hf_commit | chkpt_hash | notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | L2-7B-base | llama2 | 7  | TBD | base | `meta-llama/Llama-2-7b-hf` | LLaMA2-COMM | TBD | TBD | rope scaling TBD |
| 2 | L2-13B-base | llama2 | 13 | TBD | base | `meta-llama/Llama-2-13b-hf` | LLaMA2-COMM | TBD | TBD | ditto |
| 3 | L2-70B-base | llama2 | 70 | TBD | base | `meta-llama/Llama-2-70b-hf` | LLaMA2-COMM | TBD | TBD | ditto; requires TP>=1 on 80GB |
| 4 | L2-7B-chat | llama2 | 7  | TBD | SFT+RLHF | `meta-llama/Llama-2-7b-chat-hf` | LLaMA2-COMM | TBD | TBD | uses official chat-template |
| 5 | L2-13B-chat | llama2 | 13 | TBD | SFT+RLHF | `meta-llama/Llama-2-13b-chat-hf` | LLaMA2-COMM | TBD | TBD | ditto |
| 6 | L2-70B-chat | llama2 | 70 | TBD | SFT+RLHF | `meta-llama/Llama-2-70b-chat-hf` | LLaMA2-COMM | TBD | TBD | ditto |
| 7 | Py-1B-base | pythia | 1.0 | 0.30 (Pile) | base | `EleutherAI/pythia-1b` | Apache-2.0 | TBD | TBD | step 143000, deduped |
| 8 | Py-6.9B-base | pythia | 6.9 | 0.30 (Pile) | base | `EleutherAI/pythia-6.9b` | Apache-2.0 | TBD | TBD | step 143000 |
| 9 | Py-12B-base | pythia | 12  | 0.30 (Pile) | base | `EleutherAI/pythia-12b` | Apache-2.0 | TBD | TBD | step 143000 |
| 10 | L1-65B-base | llama1 | 65 | TBD | base | `huggyllama/llama-65b` | non-commercial | TBD | TBD | historical anchor only |

> **Pretrain token counts** for LLaMA-2 and LLaMA-1 are filled-in-place at execution from the released model cards to avoid inventing numbers; all marked `TBD` in this design.

## Per-cell notes (confounders)

### LLaMA-2 cells 1..6
- **Confounder A: pretrain compute scales with size.** All 6 share corpus but with reported differences; cell 70B received more compute than 7B. This is *the* reason Pythia is an anchor in cells 7..9.
- **Confounder B: alignment data.** Meta release notes describe an *identical SFT/RLHF recipe* across sizes, but exact data volumes and per-size RLHF rounds are not fully public. We accept Meta's claim as a working assumption and flag it as a residual confounder.
- **Tokenizer:** Sentencepiece BPE; same vocabulary across all 6 cells.
- **Prompting wraps:** cells 1..3 (base) do *not* apply the chat template; cells 4..6 apply the official Llama-2 chat template.

### Pythia cells 7..9
- **Clean pretrain control.** All three trained on The Pile, identical optimizer config, identical step 143000 (final deduped snapshot). Difference is purely parameter count.
- **Tokenizer:** EleutherAI/gpt-neox-20b BPE (different from LLaMA-2's). For this reason we compare *relative slopes across sizes*, not absolute scores against LLaMA-2.
- **No chat variant.** Pythia-DPO exists but is not part of the design (would re-introduce a third confounding data source). If at execution we want to extend RQ2 with Pythia-DPO, note it in `OPEN_QUESTIONS.md`.

### LLaMA-1-65B anchor
- **Confounder C:** older pretrain (1.4T tokens), different tokenizer (LLaMA-1 Sentencepiece), no chat alignment. Acts as a single point on the size axis showing what "another pretraining vintage" looks like in this metric space.
- **License caveat:** non-commercial research only; see `LICENSE_NOTES.md`.

## Cell × benchmark cost matrix (not executed)

Indicative pairing count to flag effort (target values, not results):

| cell | optional, logprob | generative n=5 | generative n=10 (HumanEval pass@10) | total items evaluated (TBD) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1,4 (7B) | TBD | TBD | TBD | TBD |
| 2,5 (13B) | TBD | TBD | TBD | TBD |
| 3,6 (70B) | TBD | TBD | TBD | TBD |
| 7,8,9 (Pythia) | TBD | TBD | TBD | TBD |
| 10 (LLaMA-1-65B) | TBD | TBD | TBD | TBD |

Execution effort is tracked in `reproducibility/environment_lock.md` (total GPU-hours per cell).

## Subsample agreement

To keep paired contrasts meaningful, every cell uses the **same** benchmark sample (per benchmark) for the items it has. Subsampling plan: see `benchmarks/subsampling_strategy.md`.
