{"id": "78a484f3-f0ae-4529-8de1-d54984e8f39d", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T14:16:17.026600", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "7206558e-7fae-4154-aa0e-b61dfef3df10", "action": {"command": "cat > protocol/chat_templates.md << 'EOF'
# Chat-template differences (declarative)

The design minimizes chat-template variance by limiting template use to `llama2_chat` only; all base models and Pythia receive raw text. This is intentional: comparing base and chat *within Llama-2* is one of the factors, but introducing Pythia/Llama-1 with a foreign chat template would conflate template and alignment.

## Template: Llama-2-chat

Verbatim from Meta's Llama-2-chat usage and HF tokenizer.

```
<s>[INST] <<SYS>>
{system}
<</SYS>>

{user} [/INST]
```

For multi-turn (none used in our design, except optional MT-Bench):
```
<s>[INST] <<SYS>>
{system}
<</SYS>>

{user_first} [/INST] {assistant_first} </s><s>[INST] {user_second} [/INST]
```

## Template: raw text (base models and Pythia)

```
{instruction}
```

No special tokens. The model's eos is `<</s>>` for Llama-2 chat (used as `<eos>` token); Pythia's is `<|endoftext|>`; Llama-1's is `</s>`. The decoder's stop conditions are set accordingly (see `decoding.yaml`).

## Why we don't apply a Llama-2 chat template to base models

We do not want to conflate the chat-template and the alignment recipe. Adding `[INST]…[/INST]` to a base model is *not* equivalent to "no alignment", because the base model was not post-trained to use that template. Each cell receives exactly one canonical wrap, and we do not cross-wrap.

## Multi-turn benchmarks

MT-Bench (optional) requires multi-turn chat. Pythia-base and Llama-1-65B-base are not designed for chat; if MT-Bench includes those cells, the result is reported as a separate "best-effort" stratum with the caveat that base models are not necessarily well-defined under the chat template. For this reason we *do not* apply Llama-2 chat template to Pythia or Llama-1.

## Edge cases

- `IFEval` instructions include system-like directives (e.g. "respond in JSON"). For chat cells these are still wrapped by chat template; for base cells the instruction is sent verbatim. Log per-cell format-adherence in a separate column to keep primary scoring clean.
- `TruthfulQA` MC2 is logprob-based; chat template is unused, system prompt unused.
- For `MMLU` and `ARC-C`, the standard is logprob-based multiple choice with five options. Same prompt text for chat and base; chat-template wrapping for chat cells.
- For `HumanEval`, the prompt is a code-completion task; chat-template wrapping adds 4 system tokens and may nudge formatting. Acceptable trade-off; same wrap applied to all chat cells.
EOF
