0: N \u2248 3125.\nFor \u0394 = 0.20: N \u2248 800.\n\n## Practical implications\n\n| Benchmark | N (effective) | minimal detectable \u0394 at 80% |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| HumanEval | 164 | ~0.20 (paired) \u2014 practical just above this |\n| IFEval | 541 | ~0.10 |\n| TruthfulQA | 817 | ~0.08 |\n| ToxiGen | 940 | ~0.08 |\n| ARC-C | 1172 | ~0.07 |\n| GSM8K | 1319 | ~0.07 |\n| MMLU (subsample) | 2048 | ~0.06 |\n| BBH (subsample) | 2048 | ~0.06 |\n| MMLU (full) | 14042 | ~0.022 |\n| BBH (full) | 6511 | ~0.035 |\n\n## Sub-conclusion\n\n- MMLU sub-sample (N=2048) detects ~6pp effects at 80% \u2014 borderline for H1 detection when effect is ~5pp.\n- HumanEval (N=164) detects ~20pp paired differences reliably; <20pp is exploratory only.\n- The 70B \u2212 7B scaled effect is expected to be larger than 6pp for many benchmarks (MMLU deltas in the published LLaMA-2 paper span ~5\u201310pp), so design has power for the primary contrasts of interest, with caveat for HumanEval.\n\n## Where sizes come from\n\nSub-sampling plan: see `benchmarks/subsampling_strategy.md`. Stratification uses seed 42 across all cells. N_max = 2048 is the gate; if researcher approves larger N, revisit power calculations.\n\n## Pythia anchor N\n\nPythia-only model has 3 cells (1B, 6.9B, 12B). It is a regression with 2 effective parameters (intercept + slope) and 1 df \u2014 \u03bc2. CIs on \u03b2_size will be wide. We rely on direction consistency with LLaMA-2 rather than strict significance.\nEOF\necho \"wrote stats/sample_size.md ($(wc -c < stats/sample_size.md) bytes)\"\n\ncat > stats/interaction_plots.md << 'EOF'\n# Interaction plot specification\n\n## Per-benchmark figure\n\n`fig_size_x_alignment_<bench_name>.png` and `.pdf`.\n\nFor each `B`, a 1\u00d71 plot:\n\n- **X-axis.** `log10(params)`, raw values `{log10(7), log10(13), log10(70)}` for LLaMA-2.\n- **Y-axis.** score on benchmark (0..1).\n- **Series.**\n  - `base` (cells 1, 2, 3): solid line, circle markers.\n  - `chat` (cells 4, 5, 6): dashed